<title>INDIA: India's NOCIL 1996/97 net falls.</title>
<headline>India's NOCIL 1996/97 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		598.1    vs     911.5</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   2.5    vs	 2.5</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	   4.88   vs	 7.43</p>
<p>    Sales		  11,743.3    vs   12,043.3</p>
<p>    Other income	    554.8    vs	651.1</p>
<p>    Expenditure	  10,607.4    vs   10,355.1</p>
<p>    Interest		  748.8    vs	726.7</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    941.9    vs    1,612.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    157.8    vs	137.1</p>
<p>    Tax			 186.0    vs	564.0</p>
<p>Note: National Organic Chemical Industries Ltd (NOCIL) said the decline in the company's turnover was due to lower sales volumes of petrochemical and polymer divisions consequent to the planned maintenance shutdown undertaken in March 1997.</p>
<p>The company said lower international petrochemical prices in the second half of 1996/97 affected its operations. NOCIL said its margins in petrochemical and polymer business were further affected due to the hike in input prices such as naptha.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
